1. $f$ has a right derivative $f'(x)$ at every point $x \in [a, b)$;
2. $B$ has a right derivative $B'(x)$ at every point $x \in [a, b)$;
3. $f(a) \leq B(a)$;
4. For every $x \in [a, b)$, the right derivative $f'(x) \leq B'(x)$.

Then $f(x) \leq B(x)$ for all $x \in [a, b]$.

